<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TURKU, Finland 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the ice</p>
<p>hockey world championship on Sunday:</p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>United States 5 Latvia 4 (2-1 2-0 1-3)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>United States - Donald Brashear (8:39), Brian Berard</p>
<p>(15:25), Paul Ranheim (21:35), Chris Tancill (32:41), Todd</p>
<p>Krygier (53:37)</p>
<p>Latvia - Sergei Cudinovs (9:34), Leonids Tambijevs (42:52),</p>
<p>Aleksandrs Belavskis (47:07), Andrei Ignatovics (52:20)</p>
<p>Penalties:  United States 14 minutes, Latvia 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,914</p>
<p>In Helsinki:</p>
<p>Pool A: Russia 2 Slovakia 2 (1-0 0-2 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Russia - Sergei Petrenko (00:16), Andrei Skopintsev (51:49).</p>
<p>Slovakia - Jozef Dano (30:37), Zdenko Ciger (37:42).</p>
<p>Penalties: Russia 4 minutes and Alexander Barkov 5 and 20</p>
<p>min (slashing, game misconduct), Slovakia 14 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,919.</p>
<p>Group B: Sweden 7 Canada 2 (2-0 2-0 3-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sweden - Tommy Albelin (4:28), Michael Nylander (6:55,</p>
<p>50:03), Stefan Nilsson (30:37), Magnus Arvedson (33:08), Jonas</p>
<p>Hoglund</p>
<p>(42:16), Nichlas Falk (44:11)</p>
<p>Canada - Jarome Iginla (49:47), Dean Evason (50:36)</p>
<p>Penalties: Sweden 16 minutes, Canada 55</p>
<p>Attendance: 8,396</p>
<p>In Helsinki, Group A: Finland 1 Czech Republic 2 (1-1 0-0</p>
<p>0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Finland - Mika Nieminen (08:49).</p>
<p>Czech Republic - Martin Prochazka (19:09, 41:24).</p>
<p>Penalties: Finland 4 minutes, Czech Republic 8 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,279.</p>
</text>
